and $${A^5} = \left[ {\matrix{
a & b \cr
c & d \cr

} } \right]$$, where $$i = \sqrt { - 1} $$ then which one of the following is
not true?

solution:
$$ \because $$ $$A = \left[ {\matrix{
{\cos \theta } & {i\sin \theta } \cr
{i\sin \theta } & {\cos \theta } \cr

} } \right]$$

$$ \therefore $$ $${A^n} = \left[ {\matrix{
{\cos \,n\theta } & {i\sin \,n\theta } \cr
{i\sin \,n\theta } & {\cos \,n\theta } \cr

} } \right],n \in N$$

$$ \therefore $$$${A^5} = \left[ {\matrix{
{\cos \,5\theta } & {i\sin \,5\theta } \cr
{i\sin \,5\theta } & {\cos \,5\theta } \cr

} } \right] = \left[ {\matrix{
a & b \cr
c & d \cr

} } \right]$$

$$ \therefore $$ $$a = \cos 5\theta ,\,b = i\sin 5\theta = c,\,d = \cos 5\theta $$

$$ \therefore $$ $${a^2} - {b^2} = {\cos ^2}5\theta + {\sin ^2}5\theta = 1$$

